#: 8419d70c59294b26ba0354c4fc92d543
msgid "Agent-Operable Framework Optimization"
msgstr "面向智能体操作的框架优化"

#: 8f54bfc4c28f49a18a2ca7fd8fa977a1
msgid "Status: Research proposal; not implemented"
msgstr ""

#: b2672f9425c741b59a2c6a22ead12625
msgid "Last reviewed: 2026-08-12"
msgstr ""

#: d523a4b774234da69e1f62ee50b3b7bd
msgid "Baseline: `582fc51d`"
msgstr ""

#: b5c50f768af142d59554a2fe8f330761
msgid "Owner: compiler and performance maintainers"
msgstr ""

#: 33058911644944618ada265fe85b73aa
msgid ""
"Review after: the first read-only prototype or any proposal to enable "
"automatic source/configuration changes"
msgstr ""

#: e6e09ce1caf147e99c3bdc45b838a233
msgid "Problem"
msgstr ""

#: 3ccd46a8164f4953845408201007850a
msgid ""
"Jittor already compiles and tunes operations at runtime, but optimization"
" work is difficult for an automated agent to perform safely. Relevant "
"decisions are spread across logs, generated source, tuner state, cache "
"directories, profiler output, and backend-specific flags. The information"
" is mostly human-readable, not stable enough to compare across revisions,"
" and often mixed with mutable runtime state."
msgstr ""

#: ce173d6affd84b5391ace4ee7db1ba8e
msgid ""
"The goal is to expose a narrow, versioned control and observation surface"
" so an agent can form a hypothesis, run a bounded experiment, compare "
"evidence, and produce a reviewable patch or tuning recommendation. The "
"agent must not become an unrestricted runtime autotuner or silently "
"change user execution."
msgstr ""

#: bbdbe8cf5ace4449accae2b8fc8b158f
msgid "Scope"
msgstr ""

#: 3c3ebde2a9e04cf5a11f50254ed8d0e7
msgid ""
"The proposal covers framework-internal optimization of operator fusion, "
"generated kernel choices, launch configuration, memory planning, and "
"reusable backend paths. It does not cover model architecture search, "
"training-data decisions, unreviewed package installation, or production "
"changes made without tests and a human-reviewed diff."
msgstr ""

#: d10f4df4272049318f43f1db1042b6d6
msgid "Design principles"
msgstr ""

#: 7705cddd2ea349a49dfa45c13240f322
msgid "**Read-only first.** Observation and replay land before any mutation API."
msgstr ""

#: f3f24a5e18bc4221909a4e32b6df6575
msgid ""
"**Every claim is replayable.** An experiment identifies the source "
"commit, environment fingerprint, workload, cache state, commands, and "
"metrics."
msgstr ""

#: a4abb609f7234a3fadeda4c0d074fe77
msgid ""
"**Bounded control.** A mutation declares the exact parameters or source "
"region it may change, with a timeout and resource budget."
msgstr ""

#: 472f78ac78204e8cb3ca7d3a30fcd4ae
msgid ""
"**Correctness dominates speed.** Candidate output, gradients, errors, and"
" backend placement pass before performance is compared."
msgstr ""

#: 8f08c7b11594461987caf44be902c222
msgid ""
"**No hidden fallback.** Reports state which implementation and device "
"actually executed."
msgstr ""

#: 486b79546556458ba5b44db7861c859c
msgid ""
"**Reviewable artifacts.** Source patches remain ordinary diffs; tuning "
"data is structured, small, and tied to a schema version."
msgstr ""

#: 8c29f910bb8e41318119494e60477692
msgid ""
"**Isolation by construction.** Baseline and candidate runs use separate "
"state and JIT caches."
msgstr ""

#: 247b234a12cd474088f1d42e53039535
msgid "Observation surface"
msgstr ""

#: ae3005f78d1a40c8baad463df1f87081
msgid ""
"A read-only command should emit one JSON document per workload. The first"
" schema should include:"
msgstr ""

#: c6630dca2caf4316aab85c508cb3b25b
msgid ""
"Paths stored in the document are repository-relative or artifact-"
"relative. Secrets, user home directories, host addresses, and raw "
"environment dumps are excluded. Generated source may be stored as a "
"content-addressed external artifact; the repository records only its hash"
" and a small reviewed excerpt when needed."
msgstr ""

#: 18c68e6d98fd4bdb8197af109dc7726f
msgid "Control surface"
msgstr ""

#: 22554d954ba74065a15284eb4b2de976
msgid ""
"After the observation schema is stable, a local experiment manifest may "
"permit a small allowlisted set of controls:"
msgstr ""

#: 37d955e5fa3a460cb3025e4b651da6a0
msgid "compiler/tuner flags with declared type and valid range;"
msgstr ""

#: aca3b405b394485c8a2535fa3da5d29e
msgid "fusion on/off or one named fusion-policy candidate;"
msgstr ""

#: c4aa997b549d400eac92606c8bddfd2e
msgid "launch dimensions and tile sizes within backend limits;"
msgstr ""

#: 5da322bad2cd4dcd80ae6fff59fb0a94
msgid "selection among registered implementation variants;"
msgstr ""

#: 1d0de6edeeb0423bab2c7f305335e22f
msgid "one repository patch supplied as a normal diff."
msgstr ""

#: 754144b92c3c42ceb6232d758fa576e1
msgid ""
"The runner rejects unknown keys, absolute output paths, commands outside "
"an allowlist, shared baseline/candidate caches, network access, and "
"workloads with no correctness oracle. It records the resolved controls "
"rather than only the requested values."
msgstr ""

#: 6d5c4f9388f74470ab777c92e5df5fa5
msgid ""
"The control API must not expose arbitrary Python evaluation, shell "
"fragments, or unrestricted compiler flags. Source-editing agents already "
"produce reviewable Git patches; embedding another code execution channel "
"in the optimizer would add risk without useful capability."
msgstr ""

#: 059433ae63bc4a02901131144cb86ffd
msgid "Experiment loop"
msgstr ""

#: b9bc9db0190e4cb18638f4c6c31f9a6b
msgid ""
"Each experiment changes one coherent factor. Baseline and candidate use "
"the same inputs, precision policy, synchronization, compiler toolchain, "
"device, and measurement method. Results include dispersion and sample "
"count, not only the best run. A candidate is rejected when correctness "
"fails, the requested path did not execute, compilation cost grows outside"
" budget, or the improvement is below the predeclared noise threshold."
msgstr ""

#: 2785bfcbc567441f88415ce52bde0e37
msgid "Guardrails"
msgstr ""

#: 1b3f05d5bb9c40a79c63e1f762e7f7c4
msgid ""
"Run in a disposable worktree and isolated `$JITTOR_LAB_ROOT/_state/` "
"subtree."
msgstr ""

#: d029741cea174197b004bf79c1f7ea64
msgid ""
"Require explicit CPU/accelerator parity and gradient checks for affected "
"differentiable operations."
msgstr ""

#: d5cde0998efc478eb53361f8d120c863
msgid "Cap wall time, compilation count, disk use, and generated-source size."
msgstr ""

#: 8c902fc107d64697ac1b2c59ec0ca7d4
msgid "Never reuse benchmark caches for unit tests."
msgstr ""

#: 26cfb7a40f1d4bcf94cd1da038148084
msgid ""
"Treat crashes, timeouts, NaNs, and missing metrics as failures, not zero "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: 86479d2592fa4419a7fbdc576a56fc8a
msgid ""
"Require a human-reviewed patch before any source or default policy "
"reaches the main branch."
msgstr ""

#: e2062931390846e686254fce88d05667
msgid ""
"Retain a reliable fallback and a runtime identifier for the selected fast"
" path."
msgstr ""

#: a6ef08b74266473999511856197a1fe7
msgid "Staged implementation"
msgstr ""

#: 45c1e2693bd2441a9bed0c2a33389609
msgid "Phase 0: schema and capture"
msgstr ""

#: b6f3a3d60c3344358362fb8485d9fac3
msgid ""
"Define the JSON schema, stable workload identifiers, environment "
"redaction, and a read-only capture command. Validate it on one CPU "
"elementwise operation and one CUDA matrix operation without changing "
"compilation decisions."
msgstr ""

#: 21b351a38ed2494d866c11e394a994a7
msgid "Phase 1: deterministic replay"
msgstr ""

#: 2099139be2cc469ab6dacce95d1959e5
msgid ""
"Replay a captured workload in isolated cold and warm caches. Prove that "
"operator signatures, implementation identifiers, and correctness results "
"are stable enough to compare across two worktrees."
msgstr ""

#: 4545edaed27643b5871195d628dd122f
msgid "Phase 2: allowlisted parameter search"
msgstr ""

#: 26af466fa97b40efa8c3ea96d3b3ac90
msgid ""
"Expose one existing tuner parameter family through a typed manifest. "
"Compare a small fixed candidate set and produce a report without editing "
"source or changing global defaults."
msgstr ""

#: 2d3a373acbf74c93b4d1c1e63c62b717
msgid "Phase 3: patch evaluation"
msgstr ""

#: 1ca3d911c1994e489700a3ecd75e8f5c
msgid ""
"Accept an ordinary Git diff generated outside the runner, build it in a "
"fresh worktree, and apply the same correctness/performance gate. The "
"output is a review bundle, never an automatic merge."
msgstr ""

#: 8f302b5ef87a4578b6a0577ced906314
msgid "Phase 4: policy integration"
msgstr ""

#: c55a76ba4c0d4ba3875d85b4b21003af
msgid ""
"Only after multiple reviewed studies may a winning choice enter a "
"registered runtime policy. The policy includes device guards, a fallback,"
" telemetry for path selection, and regression benchmarks."
msgstr ""

#: cd50bb77f6a741a78e834c4f5903c3ef
msgid "Initial acceptance criteria"
msgstr ""

#: 8ab750a460384e948552d49475d3627a
msgid ""
"The first prototype is successful when it can, without modifying the "
"source checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: 545f27d3686d4eb3be527400e7e97215
msgid "capture a redacted, schema-valid CPU and CUDA workload;"
msgstr ""

#: cbf2c540b3c64e52ba0e65c837887ab5
msgid "replay each workload in isolated caches;"
msgstr ""

#: 2a6b40811e2d4056a72034a6c1ec6eee
msgid "prove which implementation ran;"
msgstr ""

#: 7893704a55bc47a0827c77ba3328d515
msgid ""
"fail a deliberately wrong candidate through independent output or "
"gradient checks;"
msgstr ""

#: 937b56fe6bb549ac8f500efaeeeca5ce
msgid ""
"compare repeated latency and memory samples with a declared noise "
"threshold;"
msgstr ""

#: 4e5dd2c254374d3cbfc90432a8796bb6
msgid ""
"emit a compact report that another maintainer can reproduce from the "
"recorded commit and manifest."
msgstr ""

#: 7faabad704674c5b96680e6ee163e0a7
msgid ""
"No autonomous mutation or merge capability is in scope until these "
"criteria are met and the control surface receives a separate architecture"
" review."
msgstr ""
